{"id":"h171","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"simpleqa","question":"Who suggested the idea of shooting liquid carbon dioxide into rain clouds to induce rainfall? Is the answer \"Louis Gathmann\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"OpenAI SimpleQA (openai/simple-evals, simple_qa_test_set.csv)","claims":[{"text":"Louis Gathmann is generally credited with proposing releasing liquid CO2 into clouds to induce rain.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Gathmann developed and tested the method in the 1930s.","confidence":0.75,"lean":1,"theta":1.1781,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Gathmann's method is often cited as an early form of cloud seeding.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Historical accounts commonly credit Gathmann specifically with the liquid CO2 idea.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Gathmann's work predates Schaefer's 1946 dry-ice experiments, which are mistakenly cited as the technique's origin.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Cloud seeding broadly has multiple contributors such as Langmuir and Schaefer, so the broader question has a different answer.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Attribution details vary between sources, and the writer is relying on recall rather than a checked reference.","confidence":0.7,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.0996,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The broader-field contributors do not change the specific attribution of the liquid CO2 idea to Gathmann.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":-0.4,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":